===============================================================================
  Notes
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Comment styles
1) cited from journal article:
   !Year Authors* [Analogous reaction] [Supplemental information (e.g. pressure, calculated or estimated value (Cal./Est.), calculation method, 
    etc.)] [in the first literature which used the same analogous reaction] 
   * one author (Author's surname(AS)); two authors (AS1&AS2); three and more authors (First AS et al.)
2) cited from online model:
   !Year Model name (e.g. GRI3.0) [Analogous reaction] [Supplemental information]
3) calculated or estimated in this work:
   !Year Cal. [Supplemental information]
   !Year Est. [Analogous reaction] [Supplemental information]
2. Expressions of rate constants of ressure-dependent reactions
1) Use Troe parameters
2) Use plog parameters(If low-version Chemkin does not support plog mode, please change to pressure mode)
   For example
 C2H5+C2H3=aC3H5+CH3                           8.00E+25   -3.46    11775.0      !1986 Tsang&Hampson RRKM
  plog /  0.100                                8.00E+25   -3.46    11775.0/     !
  plog /  1.000                                3.90E+32   -5.22    19747.0/     !
  plog / 10.000                                3.90E+29   -4.24    22311.0/     !
  can be modified as:
 C2H5+C2H3=aC3H5+CH3                           8.00E+25   -3.46    11775.0      !1986 Tsang&Hampson RRKM 0.1 atm
!C2H5+C2H3=aC3H5+CH3                           3.90E+32   -5.22    19747.0/     !1986 Tsang&Hampson RRKM 1.0 atm
!C2H5+C2H3=aC3H5+CH3                           3.90E+29   -4.24    22311.0/     !1986 Tsang&Hampson RRKM 10.0 atm
